-- title:
--   Extracting aₙ via the integral Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, let $k$ be an integer with $1 \le k$, and let $n$ be a natural number with $0 < n$. The assertion is that there exists an element $t$ of [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N k ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), that is, of the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of the $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphism ring of the space `CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) k` of weight-$k$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the set consisting of the operators `heckeTLin k hℓ hℓN` for all primes $\ell$ not dividing $N$ together with the operators `heckeULin k hqN` for all primes $q$ dividing $N$ (the excluded set of primes being empty, no generator is omitted), such that for every cusp form $f$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ one has $\operatorname{qCoeff}(t f)(1) = \operatorname{qCoeff}(f)(n)$, where $\operatorname{qCoeff}(g)(m)$ denotes the coefficient of index $m$ in the $q$-expansion of $g$ taken with width $1$. Thus the $n$-th $q$-expansion coefficient functional on the whole space is realised as the first coefficient functional composed with a single integral Hecke operator; no claim of uniqueness of $t$ is made.
--
--   This is the classical identity $a_1(T_n f) = a_n(f)$ for the $n$-th Hecke operator on $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$, in the form asserting only that some element of the Hecke algebra generated over $\mathbb{Z}$ by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell \nmid N$) and the $U_q$ ($q \mid N$) extracts the $n$-th coefficient. It is used to show that the $q$-expansion coefficients separate points, which feeds the construction of an injective linear map out of a quotient of a torsion submodule of the integral lattice of cusp forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_mem_heckeAlgebra_qCoeff_one_eq_qCoeff_of_one_le.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_FLTPrelim_Modularity

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem CuspForm.exists_mem_heckeAlgebra_qCoeff_one_eq_qCoeff_of_one_le (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (k : ℤ) (hk : 1 ≤ k)
    (n : ℕ) (hn : 0 < n) :
    ∃ t ∈ CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N k (∅ : Set ℕ),
      ∀ f : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) k,
        ModularFormClass.qCoeff (t f) 1 = ModularFormClass.qCoeff f n := by sorry
